  "body": "The commit https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/a5113415d28ece380dfc3c1c3c8063ceee610745 added a new field named “[type](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#concept-sharedworkerglobalscope-type)” for `SharedWorkerGlobalScope`.\r\nBut there is already a field with the same name “[type](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#concept-workerglobalscope-type)” for `WorkerGlobalScope`.\r\n\r\nSince `SharedWorkerGlobalScope` inherits `WorkerGlobalScope`, `SharedWorkerGlobalScope` will have two fields of the same name “type”.\r\nThey are also initialized in the same [run a worker](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#run-a-worker) algorithm with the same options's type member (step 10, step 19).\r\n\r\nAre they really different fields?\r\n",
